From c07aaf250a133af1940f1e7791f8da23e32cec7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fadigah Ijesse <you@example.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:49:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix mobile font sizing and add horizontal scroll for
 dashboard tables

- variables.css: switch heading font tokens (--font-xxl/xl/lg/md) to
  clamp()-based fluid sizing so text shrinks properly on small
  screens; previous mobile override targeted a nonexistent .hero h1
  selector and never actually applied, leaving text stuck at
  desktop size
- style.css: fluid h3, remove the dead/mistargeted mobile block
- hero.css: hero heading now uses the fluid --font-xxl variable
  instead of a hardcoded 4rem
- articles.html, article.html: matching fluid sizing on page/article
  titles
- table-scroll.js (new): auto-wraps every table.data-table in a
  .table-scroll container so it can be swiped horizontally instead
  of squishing columns on mobile; works across all dashboard pages
  without touching each page's data-fetching logic
- dashboard.css: .table-scroll styling, table min-width, mobile
  edge-fade scroll hint, and a min-width:0 fix on .main-area (a
  CSS Grid item was stretching to fit wide table content instead
  of clipping it, which silently defeated the scroll container)
- dashboard/*.html: include table-scroll.js on the 8 pages that
  render data tables
